{"id": "EUVD-2026-80502", "enisaUuid": "36b6c9fb-582a-3ade-8a26-46974774895e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Avoid preempt count underflow without probe\n\nLoongArch uses break 11 for the breakpoint placed after an instruction\nthat Kprobes executes out of line. Since userspace can issue the same\nbreak instruction, do_bp() can reach kprobe_singlestep_handler() when\nthere is no current probe.\n\nThe handler actually returns false in this case, but it first calls\npreempt_enable_no_resched(). The corresponding preempt_disable() is done\nby kprobe_breakpoint_handler() on a real Kprobe hit, so it has not run\nhere. As a result, an ordinary userspace breakpoint (code 11) underflows\nthe current task's preempt count.\n\nThis also makes in_interrupt() return true until the task schedules. One\nvisible consequence is the socket cgroup attribution: cgroup_sk_alloc()\ntreats the allocation as interrupt context and assigns the socket to the\nroot cgroup. A socket opened from the SIGTRAP handler can then avoid a\nBPF_CGROUP_INET_SOCK_CREATE policy attached to the task's own cgroup.\n\nReturn as soon as kprobe_running() reports no active probe.\n\nThe same check has appeared in [PATCH v10 2/4] of the original LoongArch\nKprobes series, but was dropped before the feature reached mainline.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:35", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff40e597d5d98c0c45a4d09df8177202fac9520e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1cb727fa27c2d9c7859729cd90db7bc0f46957f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76395109a051b53860faaec96522ef08ae9e8e27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4357ebeee63cb8da1446fc936573a34e68b0f71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72ce4b24676e8b3b75376c4c559dd81c1ac52d5a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w2c5-6c3v-2hf7", "CVE-2026-89902"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b16d7c2-3ed3-3f60-ad7d-ae2a254a8378", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "0efe7546-f31a-3403-86e6-6cebb9e2926e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "1f841da5-4bc1-308a-8c52-4b45df96f390", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d4cc40fb5f58147defc6c0e9d86e6232fe31616 <76395109a051b53860faaec96522ef08ae9e8e27"}, {"id": "20d127f3-1ba5-388a-9a06-3132b342e245", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2c0c05f7-44a4-39cc-ab9d-5d86575dcbae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d4cc40fb5f58147defc6c0e9d86e6232fe31616 <c4357ebeee63cb8da1446fc936573a34e68b0f71"}, {"id": "2e73f5f8-7c14-3e25-9803-ace9cac9840f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d4cc40fb5f58147defc6c0e9d86e6232fe31616 <ff40e597d5d98c0c45a4d09df8177202fac9520e"}, {"id": "4a6738b2-c138-3902-aadf-4e1f84f21898", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d4cc40fb5f58147defc6c0e9d86e6232fe31616 <a1cb727fa27c2d9c7859729cd90db7bc0f46957f"}, {"id": "95ff7bd1-ac6e-3230-9798-2f7b57660e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d4cc40fb5f58147defc6c0e9d86e6232fe31616 <72ce4b24676e8b3b75376c4c559dd81c1ac52d5a"}, {"id": "9b51bf53-4b51-3374-adb1-ade880d07bdb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a748fafe-f6d3-3ff9-ad8b-899e532b79e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "b356054e-b82f-36c4-8c69-c5125e7d2b23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "ff9de5d5-17d6-322b-a288-b7d8d728ce9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "15160fa7-d4c0-3f3a-85f1-9e84cbb5e013", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}